<%- include('../partials/admin-top', { title }) %>

<h1>Bot settings</h1>
<p class="sub">How the bot behaves in your group and in private chats. Changes apply immediately.</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/bot">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">

  <div class="card">
    <h2>General</h2>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="enabled" name="enabled" value="1" <%= s.enabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="enabled">Bot enabled (answers messages)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="dmEnabled" name="dmEnabled" value="1" <%= s.dmEnabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="dmEnabled">Answer private (DM) messages too</label>
    </div>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="aiRephrase" name="aiRephrase" value="1" <%= s.aiRephrase ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="aiRephrase">Let the AI reword the canned replies below in fresh words each time</label>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Your saved text stays the meaning — the AI just varies the wording so the bot doesn't repeat itself. If the AI is off, busy with a real answer, slow, or changes the meaning (drops a /command, invents a question), your exact text is sent instead. Messages carrying URLs, codes or the auto-close notice are never reworded.</p>
    <label for="greetingMessage">Reply to a bare greeting ("hey", "hi") — empty = silent</label>
    <input id="greetingMessage" name="greetingMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.greetingMessage %>">

    <label for="thanksMessage">Reply to thanks ("cheers mate") — empty = silent</label>
    <input id="thanksMessage" name="thanksMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.thanksMessage %>">

    <label for="photoMessage">Reply when someone sends a photo/video/voice note the bot can't read — empty = silent</label>
    <input id="photoMessage" name="photoMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.photoMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">In private messages: any photo without a caption gets this. In the group: ONLY when the photo is a reply to one of the bot's messages — members sharing photos with each other are never interrupted. Captions are read as normal messages. Stickers and GIFs are ignored.</p>
    <p class="hint">Both work in DMs and when someone mentions or replies to the bot in the group. During problem triage, "cheers" counts as "it's fixed".</p>

    <label for="requestAckMessage">Reply when someone posts "Request: Title" ({title} — empty = silent)</label>
    <input id="requestAckMessage" name="requestAckMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.requestAckMessage %>">

    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="imdbCheck" name="imdbCheck" value="1" <%= s.imdbCheck ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="imdbCheck">Check requests against IMDb — exact hits get the proper title &amp; year, near-misses ask "did you mean …? (yes/no)"</label>
    </div>

    <label for="requestServiceQuestion">Ask which service a request is for (empty = don't ask; only when two services are named)</label>
    <input id="requestServiceQuestion" name="requestServiceQuestion" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.requestServiceQuestion %>">
    <p class="hint">The two service names come from <strong>Services &amp; login URLs</strong> above. The requester's answer is saved on the request and shown in the panel.</p>

    <label for="requestAddedMessage">Tag the requester when you Mark added in the panel ({name}, {title} — empty = silent)</label>
    <input id="requestAddedMessage" name="requestAddedMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.requestAddedMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Requests are captured to <a href="/admin/requests">VOD requests</a> automatically. "Mark added" there tags the requester in the group it came from (DM fallback).</p>

    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="ignoreAdmins" name="ignoreAdmins" value="1" <%= s.ignoreAdmins ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="ignoreAdmins">Never auto-answer admins in the group (mentions/replies to the bot still work)</label>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Even when off, admin announcements (statements addressing the group or spanning several lines) are always ignored — only an admin's actual questions get answered.</p>

    <label for="responseMode">When should the bot reply in the group?</label>
    <select id="responseMode" name="responseMode">
      <option value="mention" <%= s.responseMode === 'mention' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Only when mentioned or replied to</option>
      <option value="questions" <%= s.responseMode === 'questions' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Questions &amp; problem reports, e.g. "buffering on bbc1" (recommended)</option>
      <option value="all" <%= s.responseMode === 'all' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Try to answer every message</option>
    </select>

    <label for="cooldownSeconds">Per-user cooldown (seconds between answers to the same person)</label>
    <input id="cooldownSeconds" name="cooldownSeconds" type="number" min="0" max="600" value="<%= s.cooldownSeconds %>">
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Services &amp; login URLs</h2>
    <p class="hint">Fill these in and the bot hands out login URLs <strong>per user</strong>: a linked customer gets the URL matching their username automatically; anyone else is asked for their username first. A user on service 1 never sees service 2's URL. The URLs are kept out of the AI entirely, so it can't leak them. Empty = the flow stays off.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="serviceName1">Service 1 name (random usernames)</label>
        <input id="serviceName1" name="serviceName1" type="text" maxlength="60" value="<%= s.serviceName1 %>" placeholder="e.g. Exclusive">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="serviceUrl1">Service 1 URL</label>
        <input id="serviceUrl1" name="serviceUrl1" type="text" maxlength="200" value="<%= s.serviceUrl1 %>" placeholder="http://host:8080">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="serviceName2">Service 2 name (THM-prefixed or name-style usernames)</label>
        <input id="serviceName2" name="serviceName2" type="text" maxlength="60" value="<%= s.serviceName2 %>" placeholder="e.g. Flix">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="serviceUrl2">Service 2 URL</label>
        <input id="serviceUrl2" name="serviceUrl2" type="text" maxlength="200" value="<%= s.serviceUrl2 %>">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="servicePrefix2">Service 2 username prefix</label>
        <input id="servicePrefix2" name="servicePrefix2" type="text" maxlength="20" value="<%= s.servicePrefix2 %>">
      </div>
    </div>
    <label for="bestServiceMessage">Answer when someone asks which service is best ({name1}, {name2} — empty = let the AI dodge it)</label>
    <input id="bestServiceMessage" name="bestServiceMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.bestServiceMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Only used when both service names are set. Deliberately plugs service 1 — the AI is never allowed to invent a comparison of your own services.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Instructions (the bot's persona and rules)</h2>
    <p class="hint">This is the system prompt for the AI. Describe your app, tone, and anything the bot should or shouldn't say. FAQ entries and guides are automatically added as knowledge.</p>
    <textarea name="instructions" rows="8" maxlength="8000"><%= s.instructions %></textarea>

    <label for="faqThreshold">FAQ match strictness (0.1 loose – 0.95 strict)</label>
    <input id="faqThreshold" name="faqThreshold" type="number" step="0.05" min="0.1" max="0.95" value="<%= s.faqThreshold %>">
    <p class="hint">Above this score a FAQ answers instantly without the AI. Test scores in the <a href="/admin/faqs">FAQ manager</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Off-topic &amp; fallback</h2>
    <label for="offtopicBehavior">When someone asks something unrelated to the app</label>
    <select id="offtopicBehavior" name="offtopicBehavior">
      <option value="silent" <%= s.offtopicBehavior === 'silent' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Stay silent (recommended for groups)</option>
      <option value="redirect" <%= s.offtopicBehavior === 'redirect' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Send the short redirect message below</option>
    </select>
    <label for="offtopicMessage">Redirect message</label>
    <input id="offtopicMessage" name="offtopicMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.offtopicMessage %>">
    <label for="offtopicChatMinutes">Banter free pass: answer each user's FIRST off-topic question, then brush off for this many minutes (0 = always brush off)</label>
    <input id="offtopicChatMinutes" name="offtopicChatMinutes" type="number" min="0" max="1440" value="<%= s.offtopicChatMinutes %>">
    <p class="hint">Redirect mode only. The one-off answer is short, friendly and never asks anything back — the next off-topic question inside the window gets the redirect message above.</p>
    <label for="smallTalkSteer">Added after every one-off banter answer — pushes back to service support (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="smallTalkSteer" name="smallTalkSteer" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.smallTalkSteer %>">
    <label for="fallbackMessage">Fallback when nothing matched and the AI is off/unreachable (empty = stay silent)</label>
    <input id="fallbackMessage" name="fallbackMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.fallbackMessage %>">
    <label for="unsureMessage">When a question IS about the app but the bot can't answer it (empty = stay silent)</label>
    <input id="unsureMessage" name="unsureMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.unsureMessage %>">
    <label for="busyMessage">When the AI is overloaded — queue full or answer timed out (empty = stay silent)</label>
    <input id="busyMessage" name="busyMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.busyMessage %>">
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Problem reports</h2>
    <p class="hint">When someone reports an issue (buffering, channel down…) the bot answers with the fixes first, in the group or in a DM. A confirmed "still broken" gets further rounds of different steps (set below) before it's flagged to you (see <a href="/admin/problems">Problem reports</a> and the alert toggle in <a href="/admin/reports">Reports &amp; status</a>). 3+ different people reporting within 15 minutes triggers an outage alert immediately.</p>
    <label for="problemFollowupNote">Added to the LAST round of fixes — may promise the flag (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="problemFollowupNote" name="problemFollowupNote" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemFollowupNote %>">
    <label for="problemMoreFixesNote">Added to EARLIER rounds — a reply brings more steps, not a flag (empty = use the note above)</label>
    <input id="problemMoreFixesNote" name="problemMoreFixesNote" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemMoreFixesNote %>">
    <label for="problemFlaggedNote">Reply when a confirmed problem is flagged to you (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="problemFlaggedNote" name="problemFlaggedNote" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemFlaggedNote %>">

    <label for="problemServiceQuestion">Ask which service the escalated problem is on (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="problemServiceQuestion" name="problemServiceQuestion" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemServiceQuestion %>">
    <p class="hint">Sent together with the flagged note. The user's next reply is saved on the report and forwarded to you by DM.</p>

    <label for="problemResolvedByAdminMessage">Tell the reporter when YOU resolve their report in the panel (empty = resolve silently)</label>
    <input id="problemResolvedByAdminMessage" name="problemResolvedByAdminMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemResolvedByAdminMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Placeholders: {name} tags the reporter, {topic} is the detected symptom. Sent in the group the report came from, with a DM fallback.</p>
    <label for="problemResolvedNote">Reply when they say it's fixed ("that fixed it", "working now") (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="problemResolvedNote" name="problemResolvedNote" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemResolvedNote %>">
    <label for="problemFixRounds">Rounds of fixes before flagging to you (1 = flag on the first "still broken")</label>
    <input id="problemFixRounds" name="problemFixRounds" type="number" min="1" max="4" value="<%= s.problemFixRounds %>">
    <p class="hint">With 2 (default), the first "still broken" gets a second, different set of steps — a different link, the backup app, clearing cache, reinstalling — and only the next failure is flagged. Replies to the auto-close notice always flag immediately, as promised there.</p>
    <label for="problemNudgeMinutes">"Actually try it first" pushback: nudge instead of escalating when they confirm within this many minutes (0 = off)</label>
    <input id="problemNudgeMinutes" name="problemNudgeMinutes" type="number" min="0" max="60" value="<%= s.problemNudgeMinutes %>">
    <label for="problemNudgeMessage">The pushback message (sent at most once per report)</label>
    <input id="problemNudgeMessage" name="problemNudgeMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemNudgeMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Skipped when they give details (channel + time), say a specific check was fine ("username is right"), or when you've set a known service issue — no gaslighting during a real outage.</p>
    <label for="problemAutoCloseMinutes">Auto-close: assume silence = fixed after this many minutes (0 = off)</label>
    <input id="problemAutoCloseMinutes" name="problemAutoCloseMinutes" type="number" min="0" max="1440" value="<%= s.problemAutoCloseMinutes %>">
    <label for="problemAutoCloseMessage">Closing message (<code>{name}</code> and <code>{topic}</code> are filled in; empty = close silently)</label>
    <input id="problemAutoCloseMessage" name="problemAutoCloseMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemAutoCloseMessage %>">
    <label for="problemSoftCloseMessage">Reply to a NEUTRAL response to the closing message (empty = off)</label>
    <input id="problemSoftCloseMessage" name="problemSoftCloseMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.problemSoftCloseMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Replies to the closing message sort three ways: "still broken" phrasing is flagged to you, "all sorted" gets the resolved reply, and anything neutral ("we watched the end &amp; went to bed") gets this friendly close with the door left open.</p>
    <p class="hint">Only applies to reports that never reached you — escalated reports stay open for you to resolve. If they reply to the closing message, it goes straight to you.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Welcome message</h2>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="welcomeEnabled" name="welcomeEnabled" value="1" <%= s.welcomeEnabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="welcomeEnabled">Greet new group members</label>
    </div>
    <label for="welcomeText">Welcome text (<code>{name}</code> is replaced with the member's name)</label>
    <textarea id="welcomeText" name="welcomeText" rows="2" maxlength="1000"><%= s.welcomeText %></textarea>

    <label for="vetDays">New-member follow-up: ask me after this many days if a joiner hasn't signed up (0 = off)</label>
    <input id="vetDays" name="vetDays" type="number" min="0" max="30" value="<%= s.vetDays %>">
    <p class="hint">You'll get a Telegram DM with <strong>Keep / Remove</strong> buttons for each joiner who hasn't linked a customer account (/link) in time — Remove kicks without banning. Members who sign up in time are cleared automatically. Members can also bring a friend with <code>/invite</code> (personal one-use link, attributed to them). Requires the bot to be a <strong>group admin</strong> with invite + remove permissions.</p>
  </div>

  <p><button type="submit">Save bot settings</button></p>
</form>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Banned words</h2>
  <p class="hint">Messages containing these are never answered, and AI replies containing them are suppressed. Optionally get alerted in <a href="/admin/reports">Reports</a>.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/bot/banned-words" class="toolbar">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
    <input type="text" name="word" placeholder="Add a word or phrase…" maxlength="60" style="max-width:280px" required>
    <button type="submit" class="btn-sm">Add</button>
  </form>
  <% if (bannedWords.length) { %>
  <table class="list">
    <% for (const w of bannedWords) { %>
    <tr><td><%= w.word %></td>
      <td class="actions">
        <form method="post" action="/admin/bot/banned-words/<%= w.id %>/delete">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
          <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm">Remove</button>
        </form>
      </td></tr>
    <% } %>
  </table>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Connected chats</h2>
  <p class="hint">The bot only ever answers in chats on this list. Add a chat by sending <code>/adopt</code> in it from one of your admin Telegram IDs (set those in <a href="/admin/reports">Reports &amp; status</a>).</p>
  <% if (!allowedChats.length) { %><p class="hint">No chats connected yet.</p><% } else { %>
  <table class="list">
    <tr><th>Chat</th><th>ID</th><th>Status</th><th></th></tr>
    <% for (const c of allowedChats) { %>
    <tr>
      <td><%= c.title || '—' %></td>
      <td><code><%= c.chat_id %></code></td>
      <td><span class="badge <%= c.enabled ? 'badge-ok' : 'badge-dim' %>"><%= c.enabled ? 'enabled' : 'muted' %></span></td>
      <td class="actions">
        <form method="post" action="/admin/bot/chats/<%= c.chat_id %>/toggle">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
          <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm"><%= c.enabled ? 'Mute' : 'Enable' %></button>
        </form>
        <form method="post" action="/admin/bot/chats/<%= c.chat_id %>/delete">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
          <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm">Remove</button>
        </form>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <% } %>
  </table>
  <% } %>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/admin-bottom') %>
